From: ReadyNAS NG <readynasng@build>
Subject: [PATCH 20/23] sparc: Padre: 16 KiB pages, like the stock 2.6.17 kernel

A Linux page is 4 consecutive 4 KiB entries of the Infrant MMU
(2.6.17 CONFIG_PADRE_16K_PAGE): pte_t holds the 4 hardware words,
pte_val()/__pte() work on entry 0 (plus the A/D bits the MMU set in the
others), a table of 256 Linux PTEs is one 4 KiB hardware table.
Directories and tables are 4 KiB blocks of the uncached pool; the TLB
probe of a page covers its 4 entries; the kernel stack is one page;
AT_PAGESZ = 16384. The kernel then mounts the ext3 volumes with 16 KiB
blocks made by RAIDiator (X-RAID /c, system volume) without fuse2fs.
---
